review(698,['b13-circle'],'The original 1994 opening has one named song.',['Circle of Life is the opening number.','Hakuna Matata is not that opening number.','I Just Can\'t Wait to Be King is a separate number.','Be Prepared is a separate villain number.'],'Checked the film opening rather than album sequencing or the stage adaptation.','q164 asks lead singer; q1391 asks the opening chant words. Neither answers the song identity.')
review(699,['b13-moanasolo','b9-moanacreator'],'The 2016 heroine has a specific exploratory solo.',['How Far I\'ll Go expresses her exploratory longing.','You\'re Welcome is Maui\'s self-celebration.','Shiny is Tamatoa\'s boast.','We Know the Way concerns ancestral voyaging, not her solo.'],'Specified the 2016 solo; the ancestral ensemble also involves voyaging but cannot fit the solo performance.','q448 and q1018 ask different songs; q2543 asks the end-credit singer.')
review(700,['b13-magic'],'The magic transformation has a named Fairy Godmother song.',['Bibbidi-Bobbidi-Boo is the transformation number.','A Dream Is a Wish Your Heart Makes is Cinderella\'s song.','So This Is Love is the romantic number, not the spell.','Sing Sweet Nightingale is not the Fairy Godmother\'s spell song.'],'Distinguished the spell scene from heroine and ballroom songs; no claim about a literal single magic word.','q2361 asks its Oscar loss; q229 asks the carriage\'s original object.')
review(701,['b9-letitgo','b9-unknowncast'],'The question specifies Elsa\'s English in-story vocals.',['Menzel performs the official Elsa sequence.','Lovato recorded the separate pop/end-credit rendition.','Bell voices Anna, not Elsa.','Dion is not the credited Elsa performer.'],'End credits are part of a film, so as Elsa is essential to exclude Lovato. English excludes dubbed versions.','q450 tests a different recording in Frozen 2; q438 asks the fictional singer, not the real performer.')
review(703,['b9-ashman','b13-mermaidcatalog'],'The original 1989 lyricist is identified separately from composer.',['Ashman is the original-film lyricist.','Rice is not the lyricist for this film.','Miranda contributed to the later remake, not 1989.','Schwartz is a later Menken collaborator, not this credit.'],'The 1989 date excludes the remake\'s Miranda songs and other Menken partnerships.','q468 asks two different film credits; q159 asks the composer, not the lyricist.')
review(704,['b13-mermaidscene','b13-mermaidcatalog'],'Ariel\'s grotto solo has a distinct title.',['Part of Your World is that solo.','Under the Sea is a different number.','Kiss the Girl is a different number.','Poor Unfortunate Souls is Ursula\'s deal song.'],'Solo describes the singing, not physical solitude: Flounder and Sebastian may be present. Removed the false alone claim.','q507 asks which world interests Ariel, not the song title; q2540 concerns another film\'s production.')
review(705,['b13-beautyscene','b13-beautyopening','b9-beautysinger'],'The elaborate dinner show is one specific scene.',['Be Our Guest is the dinner presentation.','Gaston celebrates the suitor, not dinner for Belle.','Something There accompanies growing affection, not the dinner show.','Beauty and the Beast accompanies the ballroom dance.'],'Objects sing multiple songs, including the title song and Something There; only the final dinner-presentation wording excludes both.','q1255 asks the growing-affection song; q459 asks who sings the ballroom song.')
review(706,['b13-colorsscene','b13-colors'],'The heroine teaches Smith through a specific song.',['Colors of the Wind is the teaching number.','Just Around the Riverbend is a personal-choice solo.','Savages is the conflict number, not this lesson.','Listen with Your Heart is Willow\'s guidance, not Pocahontas teaching Smith.'],'Nature alone was broad enough to suggest Willow\'s song; added the singer and addressee.','q1381 asks lyricist and q2536 pop singer, both independent credits.')
review(708,['b13-bruno','b13-brunolabel'],'The chart event is fixed to 2022 and the gap since 1993.',['Bruno reached No. 1 in 2022.','Let It Go did not end the gap by reaching No. 1.','How Far I\'ll Go did not end the No. 1 gap.','A Whole New World is the 1993 predecessor, not the 2022 event.'],'Both Bruno and A Whole New World peaked at No. 1. The year and first-since clause make only Bruno defensible; removed the misleading unique-highest implication.','q2364 asks number of credited artists; q2550 asks Grammy category. Player flag retained pending publication.')
review(709,['b9-oscars1995'],'Songwriting and orchestral scoring are separate credits.',['John composed and Rice wrote lyrics for the named songs.','Menken/Ashman did not write these credited songs.','Collins/Zimmer are not the credited songwriting pair.','Zimmer alone scored rather than writing both named songs.'],'Zimmer\'s score and arrangements do not turn him into the credited John/Rice songwriters.','q453 asks the score composer; q451 asks the pop recording performer.')
review(711,['b13-distance','b13-distanceofficial','b13-hercules'],'Young Hercules has a specific belonging solo.',['Go the Distance expresses his wish to belong.','Zero to Hero is the later fame montage.','I Won\'t Say is Meg\'s romantic song.','A Star Is Born is a celebratory finale.'],'Fame and final belonging are themes elsewhere; the literal Hercules-sung desire solo selects the early number.','q2535 asks Bolton\'s pop rendition; q723 asks the separate Muses montage.')
review(712,['b13-reflection','b13-mulan'],'Mulan\'s identity-conflict solo follows the failed matchmaking visit.',['Reflection is that solo.','I\'ll Make a Man Out of You is the training number.','Honor to Us All is the bride-preparation number.','True to Your Heart is a separate soundtrack/end-title number.'],'Inner conflict alone could be broad; checked the heroine\'s actual identity solo in the original animated film.','q2537 asks the pop singer, not the in-story song identity.')
review(713,['b13-ursula','b13-mermaidcatalog','b9-ashman'],'Ursula offers Ariel a deal through a named song.',['Poor Unfortunate Souls is Carroll/Ursula\'s bargain number.','Part of Your World is Ariel\'s solo, not Ursula\'s offer.','Under the Sea is Sebastian\'s number, not the offer.','Kiss the Girl is the romance encouragement, not Ursula\'s bargain.'],'All distractors are real songs now; distinguished the bargain sequence from other performers and scenes.','q24 asks the price of the bargain; q3 villain identity, neither asks this song title.')
review(714,['b13-beautyopening'],'The village introduction is the opening sung number.',['Belle introduces the heroine and town.','Gaston is a later tavern number.','Something There is the later affection number.','Be Our Guest is the later dinner show.'],'Opening music can include the spoken prologue; the question now specifies the song introducing heroine and village.','No equivalent Belle song-identity item in the full music/film digests.')
review(715,['b13-mulan'],'English-language Shang has different speaking and singing performers.',['Osmond supplies Shang singing.','Wong supplies Shang speaking.','Chan\'s dubbed-language role does not fit the English version.','Murphy voices Mushu, not Shang.'],'Jackie Chan is a real localized Shang performer; specifying English is necessary and excludes that alternative.','q165 asks song\'s film; q871 asks character identity, not actor.')
review(716,['b13-two','b13-tarzanrecord'],'The opening montage uses one Collins song.',['Two Worlds accompanies the opening.','You\'ll Be in My Heart is the later lullaby.','Trashin\' the Camp is a later camp sequence.','Strangers Like Me accompanies later human learning.'],'Album pop versions and reprises cannot displace the opening film montage named by the sources.','q1261 asks the childhood-growth montage Son of Man, not the opening.')
review(718,['b13-1993','b9-oscars1992','b9-oscars1995'],'The ceremony year is explicit.',['A Whole New World is the 1993 winner.','Beauty and the Beast won at the 1992 ceremony.','Circle of Life was a later nominee, not the 1993 winner.','Colors of the Wind is not the recorded 1993 winner.'],'Distinguished film release year 1992 from ceremony 1993; the official unique winner excludes the later songs.','q151 asks film attribution; q2534 asks pop duo; q719 asks a different ceremony/song.')
review(719,['b13-1965'],'Mary Poppins has one original-song Oscar winner.',['Chim Chim Cher-ee is the credited winner.','A Spoonful of Sugar is not that winner.','Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious is not that winner.','Feed the Birds is not that winner.'],'The official single Song-category winner excludes the other Mary Poppins titles despite their popularity.','Sherman duo identity questions q168/q1388 do not establish which song won.')
review(720,['b13-bare'],'The individual song credit differs from other Jungle Book songs.',['Gilkyson wrote this song.','Richard Sherman wrote other film songs, not this one.','Menken is not the credited writer.','John is not the credited writer.'],'The film\'s Sherman association does not override this specific surviving Gilkyson song credit.','q1388 asks brothers\' other work; q460 asks King Louie\'s different number.')
review(721,['b13-tangled','b13-tangledcatalog'],'Rapunzel\'s tower routine is the opening solo.',['When Will My Life Begin? introduces the routine.','I See the Light is the later lantern duet.','Mother Knows Best belongs to Gothel.','Something That I Want is a separate end-credit track.'],'Removed life from the stem to avoid copying the answer; the routine and tower select the opening solo, not later dream songs.','q1266 asks the pub ensemble, q1509 the lantern duet; distinct scenes.')
