review(735,['b13-castaway'],'The Castaway Cay adults-only beach has a specific name.',['Serenity Bay is the designated beach.','Paradise Beach is not that official name.','Quiet Cove is the onboard pool designation, not the island beach.','Tranquility Bay is not the designated name.'],'Lookout Cay also has a Serenity Bay; location is specifically Castaway Cay, with Quiet Cove excluded as an onboard venue.','q975 asks onboard pool area; q977 family beach, distinct identities.',True)
review(737,['b13-arendelle','wish-dining-guide'],'Wish introduced a specific Frozen restaurant.',['Arendelle: A Frozen Dining Adventure is the documented name.','Frozen Ever After Dining is not its name.','Elsa\'s Royal Feast is not its name.','The Ice Palace Restaurant is not its name.'],'Checked full restaurant title rather than EPCOT\'s Frozen Ever After ride or another ship\'s stage show.','q415 asks count of rotational restaurants; this asks one name.',True)
review(739,['b13-icecream','b13-icecream2026'],'The described machine-dispensed dessert has a specific type.',['Soft-serve is explicitly named.','Hand-scooped gelato is not the machine dessert described.','Rolled ice cream is not the described serving method.','Mochi ice cream is a wrapped dessert, not the identified machine product.'],'Removed unsupported Dole Whip and vague parks-iconic premise. The source describes the machine product; it does not prove every other dessert is absent islandwide.','q340 identifies Aloha Isle Dole Whip; the new fact is the distinct Castaway self-service dessert.',True)
review(742,['cruise-originals','fleet-2025-table'],'The service timeline is bounded to year-end 1998.',['Only Magic was in passenger service.','Wonder did not enter service until 1999, so not two.','Dream followed in 2011, so not three.','Fantasy followed in 2012, so not four.'],'Ships ordered or under construction do not count as passenger service; this excludes Wonder\'s 1998 physical launch.','q136 asks first ship name and q137 start year; neither alone supplies a year-end fleet count.')
review(743,['cruise-originals','fleet-2025-table'],'The ship has a fixed January 2011 maiden voyage.',['Dream is the 2011 ship.','Fantasy began in 2012.','Wish began in 2022.','Treasure began in 2024.'],'Removed the needless over-a-decade superlative; maiden voyage avoids float-out ambiguity.','q1221 statue and q2276 show assignment are different ship attributes.')
review(746,['b13-snorkel','b13-snorkellist','b13-castaway'],'The submerged statues belong to a named underwater exploration area.',['The Snorkeling Lagoon contains the documented sunken Mickey statue.','Pelican Plunge is a separate waterslide platform, not the named statue-trail lagoon.','Scuttle\'s Cove is a supervised children\'s play area, not the underwater-statue location.','In Da Shade is a game pavilion, not the submerged-statue lagoon.'],'Reframed around the documented location rather than inferring that a pictured statue proves other objects never coexist underwater. Compared all four named island areas; the dedicated lagoon is distinct from the slide platform and dry play/game areas.','q427 asks run, q1211 slide structure and q747 trail rental; this tests the underwater-statue area.',True)
review(747,['b13-bikes','b13-castaway'],'One rental activity travels land pathways through tropical grounds.',['Bicycling is explicitly described along those paths.','Kayaking is water travel, not the land-path rental.','Snorkeling occurs in water, not on the paths.','Paddleboarding is water travel, not the land paths.'],'Replaced moped/scooter alternatives that could also have two wheels. All final alternatives are real outdoor activities; the land path condition excludes the water activities.','q1238 asks the island tram, not the bicycle rental.',True)
review(748,['b13-boutique'],'The onboard character-makeover salon has an official name.',['Bibbidi Bobbidi Boutique is the named salon.','The Royal Salon is not that title.','Princess Pampering Palace is not its title.','Fairytale Studio is not the identified salon.'],'The Pirates League is a package within the boutique, not a listed competing salon. No claim every package is available on every itinerary.','No other character-makeover identity question in the complete cruise digest.',True)
review(749,['b13-europa'],'Fantasy\'s adult entertainment area has a distinct official name.',['Europa is the identified area.','The District is Dream\'s area.','After Hours is used on other ships, not this district.','Serenity Bay is an island beach, not this district.'],'Same cruise line offers several adult areas; ship and European-district context select Europa.','q967 tests Dream\'s District; q968 older-ship naming. Different ship mapping required.',True)
review(750,['water-coasters'],'The poolside giant screen is named independently of an evening schedule.',['Funnel Vision is the screen name.','Starlight Cinema is not its name.','Ocean View is not its name.','Nautical Vision is not its name.'],'Removed Movies Under the Stars as though it were a DCL title; the source uses that phrase descriptively for evening viewing. Specific ship avoids fleet generalization.','q562 asks the live theatre; movie screen is a separate venue/system.',True)
review(751,['b13-thumper'],'Bambi\'s young rabbit friend is specifically named.',['Thumper is the rabbit friend.','Flower is the skunk, not the rabbit.','Friend Owl is an owl, not the rabbit.','Faline is a deer, not the rabbit.'],'The named unique rabbit identity excludes the other friends; checked Bambi rather than A Bug\'s Life\'s unrelated Thumper.','q218 identifies Flower; q2140 asks family dialogue, not this name.')
review(755,['b13-ralph'],'Ralph\'s home game is distinct from games he visits.',['Fix-It Felix Jr. is his own arcade game.','Sugar Rush is a game he visits.','Hero\'s Duty is another game he enters.','Game Central Station is the connecting hub.'],'Own means the game where he normally works as a villain; does not imply Ralph owns the physical cabinet.','q234 asks Sugar Rush, q1418 Hero\'s Duty and q843 hub; separate identities.')
review(758,['b13-northuldra'],'Yelana leads a specific named people.',['Northuldra is the named community.','Arendellians are not the Northuldra led by Yelana.','Weseltonians are not her community.','Southern Islanders are not her community.'],'Removed Forest People, a plausible descriptive synonym, and the shared trapped condition that also applied to Arendellian soldiers. Leader specifies the unique people.','q1585 asks Runeard\'s betrayal; q1097 names the river, not Yelana\'s people.')
review(760,['b13-rourke'],'The synopsis assigns the crystal theft and kidnapping to one expedition leader.',['Rourke steals the crystals and kidnaps Kida.','Vinny is not the named kidnapper commanding the theft.','Dr. Sweet is not the named commander/kidnapper.','Audrey is not the named commander/kidnapper.'],'Crew complicity does not make every crew member the leader who takes Kida. Removed commander from both stem and unique option prefix.','q2596 asks Rourke\'s deputy; q1125 demolitions expert; no repeated villain-identity item.')
review(762,['b13-bluefairy'],'The first animation of the puppet has one named magical agent.',['The Blue Fairy animates the puppet.','Tinker Bell is not the agent identified for this event.','Fairy Godmother is not the Blue Fairy.','The Good Witch is not the named agent.'],'First brings to life excludes Geppetto\'s physical construction and the later real-boy reward; removed the unnecessary second conscience-assignment fact.','q1102 asks Jiminy\'s appointed role, not the fairy\'s identity.')
review(765,['b13-lumiere'],'Lumiere\'s enchanted form is a multi-armed candle holder.',['A candelabra describes his candlestick form.','A clock is Cogsworth\'s form.','A teapot is Mrs. Potts\'s form.','A feather duster is a different servant\'s form.'],'Candlestick/candelabra terminology is compatible; clock, teapot and duster are distinct physical objects.','q284 and q17 ask other characters\' forms; q1235 requires a separate cruise restaurant mapping.')
review(770,['b13-nani'],'The original 2002 film names Lilo\'s human older sister.',['Nani is the older sister.','Pleakley is an alien agent, not her sister.','Grand Councilwoman is the alien leader, not her sister.','Cobra Bubbles is the social worker, not her sister.'],'Explicit original animated version avoids importing the remake\'s new characters; biological sister excludes a broader found-family interpretation.','q74 asks social worker, q1082 surfing friend; different relationships.')
review(771,['b13-pepita'],'Imelda has a named imposing winged wildcat spirit guide.',['Pepita is Imelda\'s winged wildcat alebrije.','Dante is the dog, not her named wildcat guide.','Ernesto is a deceased human musician.','Chicharron is a deceased human, not the winged guide.'],'Dante also becomes an alebrije; the Imelda relationship and large winged creature select Pepita specifically.','q2054 asks creature class, q2438 asks wing anatomy; neither repeats the name as answer.')
review(772,['b13-dwarfs'],'The swaying-car jewel-cavern coaster is uniquely named.',['Seven Dwarfs Mine Train is that coaster.','Big Thunder is not the specified swaying-car Snow White cavern ride.','Barnstormer is not the jewel-cavern ride.','Space Mountain is not the specified jewel-cavern ride.'],'Removed mine from the stem and replaced the non-coaster distractor; all four options now name Magic Kingdom coasters.','q1367 asks gold-rush Big Thunder, not this Snow White coaster.',True)
review(773,['b13-bayou'],'The June 2024 Magic Kingdom opening has a fixed title.',['Tiana\'s Bayou Adventure is the recorded title.','Princess and the Frog River Ride is not the official title.','Bayou Falls is not the title.','Princess Tiana\'s Journey is not the title.'],'Historical date and Florida park distinguish the later California debut; removed unbounded new-name wording.','q2219 asks drop height, not attraction identity.')
review(775,['b13-typhoon'],'The water park\'s storm-wrecked town is fictional theming.',['Typhoon Lagoon has the storm mythology.','Blizzard Beach has a ski-resort theme.','Hurricane Harbor is not this WDW park.','Stormalong Bay is a resort pool complex, not the named water park.'],'A real destructive storm is not asserted; title identifies the fictional setting rather than a weather event.','q1474 asks the ski-resort water park, a different named setting.',True)

